[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539778098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2539778098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2539778098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XYfAy","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T18:53:04Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T18:53:04Z","body":"Is it actually faster? Not sure if LocalVector can be used like this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539778098/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539834986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2539834986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2539834986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XYs5q","user":{"login":"Zylann","id":1311555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTE1NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1311555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann","html_url":"https://github.com/Zylann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T19:23:45Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T19:25:40Z","body":"I don't see why LocalVector couldn't be used like this. It has indeed potential of being faster by having the opportunity to do a single allocation to store results (instead of many for each List element), using less memory, and having better locality when iterating. It might even be possible to re-use the same LocalVector if a function uses `get_key_list` many times, saving further allocations.\r\n\r\nThough I would also be curious about a benchmark showing the difference it makes.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539834986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539945935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2539945935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2539945935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZH_P","user":{"login":"YYF233333","id":67693830,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NjkzODMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67693830?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333","html_url":"https://github.com/YYF233333","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T20:23:18Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T20:23:18Z","body":"Test function performance, for iter performance please refer to [#99936(comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99936#issuecomment-2520345383).\r\n\r\nBuild with `scons production=yes tests=yes`\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Bench Result</summary>\r\n\r\n``` bash\r\n|               ns/op |                op/s |    err% |     total | benchmark\r\n|--------------------:|--------------------:|--------:|----------:|:----------\r\n|               78.08 |       12,806,943.63 |    0.0% |      0.01 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 1`\r\n|              101.51 |        9,850,804.49 |    0.0% |      0.01 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 3`\r\n|              278.12 |        3,595,549.48 |    0.5% |      0.01 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 15`\r\n|              929.89 |        1,075,400.65 |    0.2% |      0.01 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 63`\r\n|            3,606.68 |          277,263.44 |    0.7% |      0.04 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 255`\r\n|           14,348.54 |           69,693.53 |    0.9% |      0.18 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 1023`\r\n|           60,682.36 |           16,479.25 |    0.3% |      0.72 | `LocalVector Dictionary size: 4095`\r\n\r\n|               ns/op |                op/s |    err% |     total | benchmark\r\n|--------------------:|--------------------:|--------:|----------:|:----------\r\n|              127.48 |        7,844,460.23 |    0.1% |      0.01 | `List Dictionary size: 1`\r\n|              263.94 |        3,788,777.59 |    0.1% |      0.01 | `List Dictionary size: 3`\r\n|            1,091.49 |          916,182.44 |    0.2% |      0.01 | `List Dictionary size: 15`\r\n|            4,362.40 |          229,231.49 |    0.3% |      0.05 | `List Dictionary size: 63`\r\n|           17,739.08 |           56,372.70 |    0.3% |      0.21 | `List Dictionary size: 255`\r\n|           73,570.13 |           13,592.47 |    0.3% |      0.88 | `List Dictionary size: 1023`\r\n|          300,427.36 |            3,328.59 |    0.2% |      3.59 | `List Dictionary size: 4095`\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Bench Code</summary>\r\n\r\n```C++\r\n#define ANKERL_NANOBENCH_IMPLEMENT\r\n#include \"nanobench.h\"\r\n#include \"core/templates/list.h\"\r\n#include \"core/templates/local_vector.h\"\r\n#include \"core/variant/dictionary.h\"\r\n#include <ostream>\r\n#include <sstream>\r\n\r\nclass Test\r\n{\r\n    Variant k;\r\n    Dictionary dict;\r\n\r\npublic:\r\n    void bench_get_key()\r\n    {\r\n        List<Variant> keys;\r\n        dict.get_key_list(&keys);\r\n        for (auto key : keys)\r\n        {\r\n            k = key;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    void insert_to_size(int size)\r\n    {\r\n        for (int i = dict.size(); i < size; i++)\r\n        {\r\n            Variant v = i;\r\n            dict[v] = v;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    static void bench()\r\n    {\r\n        Test test;\r\n        for (int i = 1; i < 4096 + 1; i *= 4)\r\n        {\r\n            int n = i == 1 ? 1 : i-1;\r\n            std::ostringstream name;\r\n            name << \"Dictionary size: \" << n;\r\n            test.insert_to_size(n);\r\n            auto bench = ankerl::nanobench::Bench()\r\n                .minEpochIterations(1000);\r\n            bench.run(\"List \" + name.str(), [&]{\r\n                test.bench_get_key();\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n};\r\n```\r\n</details>","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539945935/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539991302","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2539991302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2539991302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZTEG","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T20:51:53Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T20:51:53Z","body":"It's entirely possible I don't understand the technical details, but why is `LocalVector` passed as a reference by argument? Passing by argument made sense when it was a `List` pointer, but wouldn't a return value be more suitable for this new context?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539991302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539997325","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2539997325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2539997325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZUiN","user":{"login":"Zylann","id":1311555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTE1NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1311555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann","html_url":"https://github.com/Zylann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T20:55:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:11:03Z","body":"Unless I'm mistaken, returning LocalVector by value would cause an unnecessary copy of that vector (and therefore another malloc, the first one occurring inside the get_keys function before collecting keys), while passing by reference clearly avoids that copy.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2539997325/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540010987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2540010987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2540010987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZX3r","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T21:04:16Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:04:16Z","body":"Since c++17 return values like these are guaranteed to perform [copy-elision](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/copy_elision) so there should be no copying or moving into the result value, so as long as the value is only used for the return value, and the output is constructed, i.e. `LocalVector<Variant> foo = dict.get_key_list()`, there should be no additional memory operations but the result is constructed in place","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540010987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540013798","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2540013798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2540013798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZYjm","user":{"login":"Zylann","id":1311555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTE1NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1311555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann","html_url":"https://github.com/Zylann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T21:06:13Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:08:42Z","body":"Is that guaranteed even though `get_key_list` is not `inline` and `LocalVector` has no move constructor?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540013798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540018386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2540018386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2540018386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZZrS","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T21:09:21Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:11:23Z","body":"Yes it's not related to inlining, it's handled by passing the output variable in an argument I believe, so in essence it'd be like passing by reference but automated, quoting the page:\r\n> This sometimes means that even when the language syntax visually suggests a copy/move (e.g. copy initialization), no copy/move is performed — which means the type need not have an accessible copy/move constructor at all.\r\n\r\nNot sure about the super strict guarantees but generally I believe it's a safe guarantee when the return value is essentially a local temporary (it's only guaranteed when it is a `prvalue` but generally is a preferred optimization)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540018386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540020667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100333#issuecomment-2540020667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100333","id":2540020667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZaO7","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T21:11:00Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T21:11:00Z","body":"Though now that you mention it, this *could* be inlined if declared in `variant.h`, similar to the `Array` iterator functions","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540020